{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-22T04:11:32.075143Z","id":"2a364781183f80dffafcb887c47f93e7295f8249254db5206433d81a164a5ffe","body":{"detail":"Since fc43eeb6 the contract's crate docs say billing charges memory at max(memory_bytes, mem_peak_bytes): the Worker sandbox (crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs, ISOLATE_MEMORY_BYTES) reports its isolate's fixed 128 MiB as the peak. Docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 6.1 still says memory is charged at the configured limit; metering arithmetic that reads only Limits::memory_bytes undercharges every Worker run whose limit is under 128 MiB (the default is 64 MiB).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":84},"end":{"line":92},"content_hash":"ee94befd9f3a34d569280df8d13b2565f8c714f655ddf329e05e4a1f2891cff6"},"suggested_fix":"In clax-bot's metering, charge max(limits.memory_bytes, outcome.mem_peak_bytes) and say so in the spec's section 6.1.","summary":"Billing must charge the larger of Limits::memory_bytes and ScriptOutcome::mem_peak_bytes, which the run driver does not do yet","tags":["claxbot","billing","session:claude-code:7580ce1b-abf0-421d-8a2a-2be245f95865"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:35:39.592881Z","id":"4fe98cf9c1981a19391928668dc84633a7f5a7cc8f21b0545a99c7bb00eccb9e","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs (around line 345) singles out only ErrorKind::Unavailable (a stalled wait); every other error kind becomes the step's outcome for the model. InvalidOps is the host's mistake, not the script's: the model cannot fix it by writing another script, and every later script of the run would fail the same way, since the list comes from the run's surfaces. When the run loop starts passing a list (Script::with_ops), it should check the list itself with clax_bot_sandbox::validate_ops before the first step, or treat InvalidOps as ending the run, rather than spend steps on it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":594},"end":{"line":597},"content_hash":"d4a9e157566ac22698c212a3ed7484b1940bbf84c4f7d2522207fa13540ab63c"},"summary":"A run whose script carries a list validate_ops refuses ends with ErrorKind::InvalidOps, which crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs treats like any script error: the step fails and the model reads the message","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:35:39.593033Z","id":"b5e2a69175c9e5c279d2a1294813762cf49d4593b31603ced512562e29946d1a","body":{"detail":"clax_surface::Limits (crates/clax-surface/src/limits.rs) bounds one surface: 256 operations, names of 64 bytes, namespaces 32 deep by default and up to MAX_DEPTH 64. The sandbox bounds one script's whole list: 4096 names, 4096 bytes a dotted name, 256 KiB together. Seventeen full surfaces in one run pass 4096 names; a surface read with depth raised to 64 can have a dotted name of 64 + 64 x 65 + 64 bytes, over 4096. Either is refused with ErrorKind::InvalidOps only when a script runs. The sandbox's bounds are what keep the prelude's work and the job's size bounded on their own; the check that a run's surfaces fit them belongs where the run's list is put together, before the run starts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":312},"end":{"line":317},"content_hash":"aa5798dc04e68cd5498f9368fe2cf8d9cb3fcec0e5b0d663c5c8ede931ff01ed"},"summary":"MAX_OPS, MAX_OP_BYTES and MAX_OPS_BYTES are not derived from clax-surface's Limits, so a list made of definitions that each pass crates/clax-surface/src/check.rs can still be refused at run time","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:35:39.593115Z","id":"442354b9424286b2f73c0d978029e68f495090b3f5a19e976fd4df274abd086c","body":{"detail":"With a list, each run copies it: QuickJS into an Arc and a HashSet (crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs, Sandbox::run) beside the copy Engine's script clone makes, the Worker into RunState's set and the job's JSON. That is at most 256 KiB (MAX_OPS_BYTES) a step, small beside a fresh QuickJS runtime or isolate per step, and nothing for a script without a list. An Arc would need serde's rc feature (a Cargo.toml change and bazel-sync) and a list type the run loop holds as Arc.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":136},"end":{"line":143},"content_hash":"33be7d1932b7b022790a8a7207c307abccebfb038ebb56ce9b3e2e8a9d9367f5"},"summary":"Script::ops as an Arc<[String]> shared by every step of a run, instead of a Vec<String> each step copies","tags":["revisit:a profile of a run step shows copying the operation list matters","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:46:04.141479Z","id":"31088a7a6e01495eeacf342683456ffbe815665fc8cc125eb40b1c217aed6fac","body":{"detail":"Both sandboxes call Host::ask (crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs, crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/loader.rs), whose default wraps Host::call in HostReply::Answer, so the existing impls (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs StepHost, crates/clax-bot/src/script_reference.rs RunHost, and the test hosts in crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs, crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs and crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs) compile unchanged. Two methods let a host implement both inconsistently: a host overriding ask decides what its call returns for a waiting call (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/conformance.rs ScriptedHost::call turns Waiting into a host error). One method returning HostReply leaves one answer per call.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":555},"end":{"line":565},"content_hash":"f9c47b0ff72cd521fe00b6fc0f48a8cd111955b540a27277c4ceb66b47657288"},"summary":"Host::call itself returns HostReply, instead of a provided Host::ask beside it","tags":["revisit:the run loop's StepHost is the only Host outside the sandbox crates and their tests","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:46:44.949558Z","id":"bdc567c5fe2d9df1d655c544b468421c86e0fff3b4b096178b8ff5ddd70278c7","body":{"detail":"Since fc43eeb6 the contract's crate docs say billing charges memory at max(memory_bytes, mem_peak_bytes): the Worker sandbox (crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/mod.rs, ISOLATE_MEMORY_BYTES) reports its isolate's fixed 128 MiB as the peak. Docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-21-claxbot-design.md section 6.1 still says memory is charged at the configured limit; metering arithmetic that reads only Limits::memory_bytes undercharges every Worker run whose limit is under 128 MiB (the default is 64 MiB).","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":111},"end":{"line":119},"content_hash":"ee94befd9f3a34d569280df8d13b2565f8c714f655ddf329e05e4a1f2891cff6"},"suggested_fix":"In clax-bot's metering, charge max(limits.memory_bytes, outcome.mem_peak_bytes) and say so in the spec's section 6.1.","summary":"Billing must charge the larger of Limits::memory_bytes and ScriptOutcome::mem_peak_bytes, which the run driver does not do yet","supersedes":"2a364781183f80dffafcb887c47f93e7295f8249254db5206433d81a164a5ffe","tags":["claxbot","billing","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:46:45.188417Z","id":"3ccc6148fb7ce41a2aad2d9ffcc5c33f987df570b6730534bfd32fa5f0ce4348","body":{"detail":"With a list, each run copies it: QuickJS into an Arc and a HashSet (crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs, Sandbox::run) beside the copy Engine's script clone makes, the Worker into RunState's set and the job's JSON. That is at most 256 KiB (MAX_OPS_BYTES) a step, small beside a fresh QuickJS runtime or isolate per step, and nothing for a script without a list. An Arc would need serde's rc feature (a Cargo.toml change and bazel-sync) and a list type the run loop holds as Arc.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":156},"end":{"line":163},"content_hash":"33be7d1932b7b022790a8a7207c307abccebfb038ebb56ce9b3e2e8a9d9367f5"},"summary":"Script::ops as an Arc<[String]> shared by every step of a run, instead of a Vec<String> each step copies","supersedes":"442354b9424286b2f73c0d978029e68f495090b3f5a19e976fd4df274abd086c","tags":["revisit:a profile of a run step shows copying the operation list matters","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:46:45.379338Z","id":"97fa4e012036ea0f98b1766df08e5dfdec89b7053cdb13a7a8ff234cba7c5e80","body":{"detail":"clax_surface::Limits (crates/clax-surface/src/limits.rs) bounds one surface: 256 operations, names of 64 bytes, namespaces 32 deep by default and up to MAX_DEPTH 64. The sandbox bounds one script's whole list: 4096 names, 4096 bytes a dotted name, 256 KiB together. Seventeen full surfaces in one run pass 4096 names; a surface read with depth raised to 64 can have a dotted name of 64 + 64 x 65 + 64 bytes, over 4096. Either is refused with ErrorKind::InvalidOps only when a script runs. The sandbox's bounds are what keep the prelude's work and the job's size bounded on their own; the check that a run's surfaces fit them belongs where the run's list is put together, before the run starts.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":332},"end":{"line":337},"content_hash":"aa5798dc04e68cd5498f9368fe2cf8d9cb3fcec0e5b0d663c5c8ede931ff01ed"},"summary":"MAX_OPS, MAX_OP_BYTES and MAX_OPS_BYTES are not derived from clax-surface's Limits, so a list made of definitions that each pass crates/clax-surface/src/check.rs can still be refused at run time","supersedes":"b5e2a69175c9e5c279d2a1294813762cf49d4593b31603ced512562e29946d1a","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T19:46:45.546518Z","id":"53c6a8a73b624f63e48203f11c590dd03da73feadb21a7eeb084c89eebedcf80","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs (around line 345) singles out only ErrorKind::Unavailable (a stalled wait); every other error kind becomes the step's outcome for the model. InvalidOps is the host's mistake, not the script's: the model cannot fix it by writing another script, and every later script of the run would fail the same way, since the list comes from the run's surfaces. When the run loop starts passing a list (Script::with_ops), it should check the list itself with clax_bot_sandbox::validate_ops before the first step, or treat InvalidOps as ending the run, rather than spend steps on it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":635},"end":{"line":638},"content_hash":"d4a9e157566ac22698c212a3ed7484b1940bbf84c4f7d2522207fa13540ab63c"},"summary":"A run whose script carries a list validate_ops refuses ends with ErrorKind::InvalidOps, which crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs treats like any script error: the step fails and the model reads the message","supersedes":"4fe98cf9c1981a19391928668dc84633a7f5a7cc8f21b0545a99c7bb00eccb9e","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T21:35:40.598457Z","id":"f10b2c3b497f2a525ee9fe5f07e04a320f1d03fa4d1b9f2aaf02b064657f581e","body":{"detail":"`Tick::script` (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs) takes the list from `RunSurfaces::operations` (crates/clax-bot/src/registry.rs), checks it with `clax_bot_sandbox::validate_ops` before `begin_step`, and ends the run with `Ending::failed(CODE_OPS_INVALID, …)`; a sandbox that answers `ErrorKind::InvalidOps` all the same (a stricter one) is treated the same after the run, with the sessions dropped. The model is shown no step for it: `generic::a_run_whose_surfaces_operations_are_not_usable_fails_and_takes_no_script_step`. For a run whose one binding is `clax` the list is `clax_bot::api::op_names()` (`generic::a_runs_scripts_are_given_the_operations_of_its_surfaces`).","kind":"comment","references":"53c6a8a73b624f63e48203f11c590dd03da73feadb21a7eeb084c89eebedcf80","summary":"The run loop now passes each script its run's operations and ends the run `failed` (`surface_ops_invalid`) for a list `validate_ops` refuses, before the step is begun","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T22:57:43.869158Z","id":"45b80e72f84d682e4aa8de1d9d11680768123ff3d76d37983ee3a156b9dedc24","body":{"detail":"`then` is refused because `await` calls it. The namespaces of `clax` have no prototype (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js:75), so an operation with one of these names is the only property of that name: `console.log(clax.desk)` and a script's returned value go through `JSON.stringify` (prelude.js:49, 166), which calls `toJSON(\"\")`, and `` `${clax.desk}` `` calls `toString()` then `valueOf()`. Each such call is a call of the host's operation that the script did not write (the run loop still checks its arguments), and for `toString` the coercion then throws a TypeError, since the call's promise is no primitive. `clax_surface` accepts all three as an operation's and as a namespace's name (`callable`, crates/clax-surface/src/allow.rs:47; probed: a host's file with `toJSON(): Promise<null>` reads), and so does `validate_ops`. The JavaScript side is read from prelude.js, not run.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":339},"end":{"line":342},"content_hash":"b4af7771e2d30da65aa488aeb7bcb51c517879c60bb10d97175e0e050751b7f1"},"suggested_fix":"Add `toJSON`, `toString` and `valueOf` to `RESERVED_SEGMENTS`, to the prelude's and the Worker driver's own checks and to `clax_surface`'s `callable`.","summary":"`toJSON`, `toString` and `valueOf` are usable as an operation's name, and are then called by JavaScript itself when a script logs, returns or concatenates the namespace that holds them","tags":["security","review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-11T23:14:20.943735Z","id":"52ae8d48ccd2e9aac22708ac22a325d94acbca61aa0ddd5c9bd6d5c64564e906","body":{"detail":"The list is `clax_surface::RESERVED_CALLABLE` (crates/clax-surface/src/allow.rs): `__proto__`, `constructor`, `prototype`, `then`, `toJSON`, `toString`, `toLocaleString`, `valueOf`, `hasOwnProperty`, `isPrototypeOf`, `propertyIsEnumerable`, `__defineGetter__`, `__defineSetter__`, `__lookupGetter__`, `__lookupSetter__`. `callable` (operations, namespaces, allow patterns) refuses each in both notations for both authors; crates/clax-bot/src/clax.d.ts uses none. `clax_bot_sandbox::RESERVED_SEGMENTS` is the same list (clax-bot-sandbox may not depend on clax-surface; crates/clax-bot/src/api.rs `the_sandbox_reserves_the_names_the_surface_format_does` holds them equal), and src/prelude.js refuses each by a `switch` that the sandbox's own test holds names every one. Tests: crates/clax-surface/src/tests/refusals.rs (a `.d.ts` operation and namespace of each name) and tests/manifest.rs (a manifest operation and namespace of each name); crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/conformance.rs gains twelve `refused_list` cases (`shell.toJSON` … `shell.__lookupSetter__`, `toLocaleString`, `toJSON.read`), run by clax-bot-js and by the Worker's `sandbox_test`. Fields of an interface may still be named so: a value's `toJSON` field is data, not a function, and `JSON.stringify` calls only a function. Left for the owner to close.","kind":"comment","references":"45b80e72f84d682e4aa8de1d9d11680768123ff3d76d37983ee3a156b9dedc24","summary":"Fixed: `toJSON` and the methods of `Object.prototype` are refused beside `then` as an operation's or a namespace's name, by `clax-surface`, `validate_ops` and the prelude, from one list","tags":["security","claxbot-surfaces","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:54:02.022809Z","id":"0033a648dd35f31e8f4f815bf6db3c0f77a5c9a57457002a618ee3e180b02e30","body":{"detail":"`then` is refused because `await` calls it. The namespaces of `clax` have no prototype (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/prelude.js:75), so an operation with one of these names is the only property of that name: `console.log(clax.desk)` and a script's returned value go through `JSON.stringify` (prelude.js:49, 166), which calls `toJSON(\"\")`, and `` `${clax.desk}` `` calls `toString()` then `valueOf()`. Each such call is a call of the host's operation that the script did not write (the run loop still checks its arguments), and for `toString` the coercion then throws a TypeError, since the call's promise is no primitive. `clax_surface` accepts all three as an operation's and as a namespace's name (`callable`, crates/clax-surface/src/allow.rs:47; probed: a host's file with `toJSON(): Promise<null>` reads), and so does `validate_ops`. The JavaScript side is read from prelude.js, not run.","kind":"suggestion","span":{"start":{"line":338},"end":{"line":365},"content_hash":"cd0c3f17d8c0eee8d2a9f290effceb1d2ac5cf505ceb8ad5f1b79fa6be868513"},"suggested_fix":"Add `toJSON`, `toString` and `valueOf` to `RESERVED_SEGMENTS`, to the prelude's and the Worker driver's own checks and to `clax_surface`'s `callable`.","summary":"`toJSON`, `toString` and `valueOf` are usable as an operation's name, and are then called by JavaScript itself when a script logs, returns or concatenates the namespace that holds them","supersedes":"45b80e72f84d682e4aa8de1d9d11680768123ff3d76d37983ee3a156b9dedc24","tags":["security","review","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:54:02.320955Z","id":"ad2e5beda061015ebb5013c8225d25d0d8acc05a7cd7d414be69c94013d9fc49","body":{"detail":"Both sandboxes call Host::ask (crates/clax-bot-js/src/lib.rs, crates/clax-worker/src/sandbox/loader.rs), whose default wraps Host::call in HostReply::Answer, so the existing impls (crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs StepHost, crates/clax-bot/src/script_reference.rs RunHost, and the test hosts in crates/clax-bot/src/script_differential.rs, crates/clax-bot/tests/seam.rs and crates/clax-bot/tests/web.rs) compile unchanged. Two methods let a host implement both inconsistently: a host overriding ask decides what its call returns for a waiting call (crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/conformance.rs ScriptedHost::call turns Waiting into a host error). One method returning HostReply leaves one answer per call.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":578},"end":{"line":588},"content_hash":"f9c47b0ff72cd521fe00b6fc0f48a8cd111955b540a27277c4ceb66b47657288"},"summary":"Host::call itself returns HostReply, instead of a provided Host::ask beside it","supersedes":"31088a7a6e01495eeacf342683456ffbe815665fc8cc125eb40b1c217aed6fac","tags":["revisit:the run loop's StepHost is the only Host outside the sandbox crates and their tests","session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/clax-bot-sandbox/src/lib.rs","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-11-12T00:54:02.633391Z","id":"f08a77b85891b8d97d98f4b6ce448d247e197981e93c6175fcdda86ce1317a67","body":{"detail":"crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs (around line 345) singles out only ErrorKind::Unavailable (a stalled wait); every other error kind becomes the step's outcome for the model. InvalidOps is the host's mistake, not the script's: the model cannot fix it by writing another script, and every later script of the run would fail the same way, since the list comes from the run's surfaces. When the run loop starts passing a list (Script::with_ops), it should check the list itself with clax_bot_sandbox::validate_ops before the first step, or treat InvalidOps as ending the run, rather than spend steps on it.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":658},"end":{"line":661},"content_hash":"d4a9e157566ac22698c212a3ed7484b1940bbf84c4f7d2522207fa13540ab63c"},"summary":"A run whose script carries a list validate_ops refuses ends with ErrorKind::InvalidOps, which crates/clax-bot/src/script.rs treats like any script error: the step fails and the model reads the message","supersedes":"53c6a8a73b624f63e48203f11c590dd03da73feadb21a7eeb084c89eebedcf80","tags":["session:claude-code:443e6ffa-9215-48fe-9313-5be76354ae11"]}}
